  "final_message": "Done. The sensor dashboard is complete:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 Flask + SQLite in `./data/app.db`:\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 + Bearer token; tokens stored hashed)\n- `GET/POST /api/sensors` (sorted by name; owner-only creation), `GET/DELETE /api/sensors/{id}` (owner-only delete cascades readings)\n- `GET/POST /api/sensors/{id}/readings` (`{\"items\", \"total\"}`, newest first, `limit` support; owner-only posting, server-set `recorded_at`, updates `last_value`/`last_updated`)\n- 401 without valid token, 403 for foreign sensors, JSON errors under `/api`, serves `frontend/dist` with SPA fallback\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/` \u2014 React + TS + Vite + Tailwind v4):\n- Register/sign-in forms, signed-in username + sign-out in the header\n- Sensor cards (latest value, unit, location, \"updated X ago\") polling every 10 s\n- Sensor page (`/sensors/{id}`) with hand-rolled SVG line chart + readings table showing total\n- Sensor registration, reading posting, and delete with inline confirm \u2014 all owner-scoped\n\n**Verified**: 59/59 API checks (auth, ownership, pagination, cascade delete, error cases), `tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm ci && npm run build` works from the lockfile, and the Dockerfile's `pip install -r \u2026 -c \u2026` step now works \u2014 `requirements.txt` needed hash pins since pip ignores hashes from constraints files. Data survives restarts.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
